8:## Unreleased
9-
10-- feat: route the GitHub REST client and the GH-token preflight through `bborbe/http`'s rate-limit retry round tripper (`github.com/bborbe/http` v1.28.1), so a 403/429 from `api.github.com` is retried after the server-requested wait instead of ending the work item; waits over the five-second `MaxWait` bound are deferred so the caller sees the real rate-limit response rather than a context-deadline error
11-
12-## v0.8.7
13-
14-- chore: remove orphaned section comments left in `.trivyignore` by the stale-ignore sweep
15-
16-## v0.8.6
17-
18-- chore: remove 10 stale vulnerability ignores (withdrawn advisory, module absent from go.mod, or version outside the affected range)
19-
20-## v0.8.5
21-
22-- fix: bump the baked dark-factory pin from `v0.199.6` to `v0.199.7`, which stashes the dirty spec bookkeeping around the branch workflow's `git merge origin/<default>` sync. `syncWithRemoteViaDeps` fetched and merged before `setupInPlaceBranch` persisted the generator's spec-status write, so `git merge` aborted with `Your local changes to the following files would be overwritten by merge: specs/in-progress/…`; the prompt failed permanently, the lifecycle drain aborted, and the agent exited 1 — surfaced as a bare `pod_crash_no_stdout`. `syncWithRemoteViaDeps` now stashes `SpecBookkeepingPrefixes` before the merge and pops after. Both the CLI build and the plugin marketplace clone move together, since they are pinned to the same `DARK_FACTORY_VERSION`.
