## Improvements

- [PROMPT] Requirement 3 claims the `Retry-After: 1` accumulation case "fails at `MaxWait: 5s` and passes at `1s`". It does not: the library retries when `wait <= MaxWait` (strict-greater defers), so at 5s it sleeps 5 × 1s = 5s, still well inside the 15s client timeout. A discriminating case needs `Retry-After: 5` (5 × 5s = 25s > 15s at the old bound; deferred immediately at 1s). The test was added as literally specified, but it cannot distinguish the two bounds.
- [GUIDE] Worth recording in the retry-library usage notes: `MaxWait` is a per-wait cap with an inclusive comparison, so the total budget is `MaxAttempts × MaxWait` and a bound only helps if the per-attempt wait is near it.
[15:25:54] result: All requirements implemented and verified.

